# Resolved by `op run` when tools/directories.py asks YouTube and Spotify
# where each episode is. Committed on purpose: every op:// below is a
# REFERENCE, not a value.
#
#   op run --env-file=tools/directories.env -- ./tools/directories.py
#
# YouTube: the same client and channel token the publisher uploads with
# (tools/youtube.env), read here to list the channel's own uploads.
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=op://Engineering/YouTube podcast client/username
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=op://Engineering/YouTube podcast client/credential
YOUTUBE_REFRESH_TOKEN=op://Engineering/YouTube podcast token/credential
# Spotify: an app made at developer.spotify.com/dashboard, any name, no
# redirect URI used (the client credentials flow reads the public catalogue
# and nothing of any user). Since March 2026 the account that owns the app
# must hold Premium, or the app stops answering. One API Credential item.
# Uncomment once the item exists: op run refuses to start while a reference
# below has nothing to resolve to.
#SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=op://Engineering/Spotify podcast app/username
#SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=op://Engineering/Spotify podcast app/credential
